window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-27d47d73cc460564"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"understand-large-codebases\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">理解大型代码库</h1> <p>梳理请求流转、绘制陌生模块地图，并快速找到该读的文件。</p> <p>使用 Codex 梳理陌生代码库，解释不同模块及数据流，并在你编辑前指出值得继续阅读的文件。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>刚加入新仓库或服务的新工程师。</li> <li>想在修改某项功能前先了解它如何工作的任何人。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>解释我需要了解的系统部分</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请解释请求在代码库的 &lt;name of the system area&gt;（系统区域名称）中如何流转。\n\n请包括：\n\n- 各模块分别负责什么\n- 数据在哪里验证\n- 修改前需要注意的主要陷阱\n\n最后列出我接下来应该阅读的文件。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT 桌面应用</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">简介</h2> <p>刚加入一个代码仓库，或突然接手陌生功能时，Codex 可以在你开始修改代码前帮你熟悉项目。目标不只是得到高层摘要，还要梳理请求流转、理解各模块分别负责什么，并找出接下来值得阅读的文件。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">使用方法</h2> <p>如果你刚加入一个项目，可以直接请 Codex 介绍整个代码库：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Explain this repo to me\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">向我解释这个仓库。</div></div> <p>如果你要为现有代码库添加功能，可以请 Codex 解释某个具体系统区域。范围说得越清楚，解释就越具体：</p> <ol> <li>告诉 Codex 你希望了解的相关文件、目录或功能区域。</li> <li>请它追踪请求流转，并解释哪些模块负责业务逻辑、传输、持久化或 UI。</li> <li>在修改前询问验证、外部副作用或状态转换发生在哪里。</li> <li>最后询问接下来应该阅读哪些文件，以及有哪些风险点。</li> </ol> <p>有用的入门说明应提供一张具体地图，而不只是文件名列表。到最后，Codex 应解释主要流程、指出风险部分，并告诉你开始修改前应阅读哪些文件或运行哪些检查。</p> <p><a id=\"questions-to-ask-next\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">接下来可以问什么</h2> <p>Codex 给出第一版解释后，继续追问，直到内容具体到让你有信心进行第一次修改。好的后续问题通常会要求它指出假设、隐藏依赖，以及修改后重要的检查。</p> <ul> <li>哪个模块负责实际业务逻辑，哪个模块负责传输或 UI 层？</li> <li>验证在哪里发生？它会强制执行哪些假设？</li> <li>修改这条流程时，哪些相关文件或后台任务容易被漏掉？</li> <li>修改这个区域后，我应该运行哪些测试或检查？</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"understand-large-codebases\">Understand large codebases</h1> <p>Trace request flows, map unfamiliar modules, and find the right files fast.</p> <p>Use Codex to map unfamiliar codebases, explain different modules and data flow, and point you to the next files worth reading before you edit.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>New engineers onboarding to a new repo or service</li> <li>Anyone trying to understand how a feature works before changing it</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Explain the System Area I Need</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Explain how the request flows through &lt;name of the system area&gt; in the codebase.\n\nInclude:\n- which modules own what\n- where data is validated\n- the top gotchas to watch for before making changes\n\nEnd with the files I should read next.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT desktop app</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>When you are new to a repo or dropped into an unfamiliar feature, Codex can help you get oriented before you start changing code. The goal is not just to get a high-level summary, but to map the request flow, understand which modules own what, and identify the next files worth reading.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <p>If you're new to a project, you can simply start by asking Codex to explain the whole codebase:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Explain this repo to me\n</code></pre> <p>If you need to contribute a new feature to an existing codebase, you can ask codex to explain a specific system area. The better you scope the request, the more concrete the explanation will be:</p> <ol> <li>Give Codex the relevant files, directories, or feature area you are trying to understand.</li> <li>Ask it to trace the request flow and explain which modules own the business logic, transport, persistence, or UI.</li> <li>Ask where validation, side effects, or state transitions happen before you edit anything.</li> <li>End by asking which files you should read next and what the risky spots are.</li> </ol> <p>A useful onboarding answer should leave you with a concrete map, not just a list of filenames. By the end, Codex should have explained the main flow, highlighted the risky parts, and pointed you to the next files or checks that matter before you start editing.</p> <h2 id=\"questions-to-ask-next\">Questions to ask next</h2> <p>Once Codex gives you a first pass, keep going until the explanation is specific enough that you would trust yourself to make the first edit. Good follow-up questions usually force it to call out assumptions, hidden dependencies, and the checks that matter after a change.</p> <ul> <li>Which module owns the actual business logic versus the transport or UI layer?</li> <li>Where does validation happen, and what assumptions are enforced there?</li> <li>What related files or background jobs are easy to miss if I change this flow?</li> <li>Which tests or checks should I run after editing this area?</li> </ul>"};
